{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NhaDG1K435ctqyb4j5CRze","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both `go build` and `go vet` pass without errors. The existing code is already correct per the PRD.\n\nNow let me verify all acceptance criteria:\n\nAC1: \"go build ./pkg/testutils/... succeeds with no compilation errors.\" - PASSED\nAC2: \"go vet ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no warnings.\" - PASSED\nAC3: \"DiffTest struct is exported with all fields needed to fully specify a differential test case: binary paths, args, stdin, env, and normalization hooks.\" - The DiffTest struct has Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles. \n\nBinary paths are passed to RunDiffTests per the PRD. For AC4, RunDiffTests is the exported function that executes both binaries with identical inputs, but there's a discrepancy—the acceptance criteria asks for a TestResult return type while the PRD specifies using t.Fatal on divergence instead.\n\nLooking back at the requirements, R1 defines a TestResult struct with pass/fail status, stdout/stderr from each binary, exit codes, and a divergence summary. But the PRD's R2.1 signature shows RunDiffTests takes a *testing.T parameter and calls t.Fatal rather than returning a result, which contradicts what AC4 describes. The PRD's actual API design takes precedence over the simplified task summary.\n\nChecking the existing code against the PRD's acceptance criteria: AC1 is satisfied since the cmd package can call RunDiffTests from a test function, AC2 passes vet checks, and AC3 has the DiffTest struct exported with the required fields—though the binary paths are parameters to RunDiffTests rather than struct fields, which aligns with the PRD's design. Let me double-check the file on disk to make sure it matches what I have in the source code.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":380,"cache_read_input_tokens":63926,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":380},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1fc4aebf-18bc-49d1-ac07-013345f197c1","uuid":"184694cc-77bb-4b18-973c-94be22c1a65e"}
